# 5. Installing Boto3

Kali Linux protects its system Python environment, so Boto3 should be installed inside a virtual environment.

### Create Virtual Environment

```bash
python3 -m venv venv
```

### Activate Virtual Environment

```bash
source venv/bin/activate
```

After activation:

```text
(venv) kali@kali:~/boto3-practice$
```

### Install Boto3

```bash
pip install boto3
```

### Verify Installation

```bash
python -c "import boto3; print(boto3.__version__)"
```

Example:

```text
1.43.83
```

